{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":343041,"duration_api_ms":342980,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs. Re-implementations diverge on edge cases. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity via differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (utilities), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets).\n\n**Current state**: Specs are complete for all rel00.0 use cases. `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` exists on the working branch. No other generated code is on the working branch (previous generation lives at `generation-merged` tags). Four rel00.0 use cases have code status \"not started\": magefiles, format, sys, testutils (testutils has code via source_code).\n\n**Current release**: rel00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure). Remaining use cases: uc001-magefiles, uc002-format, uc003-sys (uc004-testutils already has code).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nWithin rel00.0, dependency order is: `pkg/sys` → `pkg/format` (format may depend on sys for terminal size queries used in column alignment) → `magefiles` (consumer of all libraries). Since `pkg/testutils` already exists, the next piece is `pkg/sys` — the lowest-level abstraction layer that other packages build on.\n\nPer P2, implementation and tests are split into separate tasks. This task covers implementation only.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/sys file metadata and terminal size abstractions (rel00.0-uc003)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/sys component -- responsibilities, capabilities, technology choices section for golang.org/x/sys)\n      - \"docs/specs/product-requirements/ (glob for prd*sys*.yaml -- read the PRD for pkg/sys to identify requirement IDs and struct shapes)\"\n      - \"docs/specs/use-cases/ (glob for *uc*sys*.yaml -- read the use case for pkg/sys)\"\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (coding style reference -- copyright header, SPDX identifier, package doc comment with Implements tag)\n      - go.mod (check if golang.org/x/sys dependency already exists; add it if not)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"FileInfo struct with platform-independent fields (ModTime, AccessTime, Blocks, BlockSize, underlying os.FileInfo); Stat and Lstat functions returning (*FileInfo, error)\"\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo_darwin.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Darwin-specific extraction from syscall.Stat_t (Mtimespec, Atimespec, Blocks fields)\"\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo_linux.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Linux-specific extraction from syscall.Stat_t (Mtim, Atim, Blocks fields)\"\n      - path: pkg/sys/terminal.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"WinSize struct and TerminalSize function using TIOCGWINSZ ioctl\"\n      - path: pkg/sys/doc.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Package documentation with Implements tag referencing PRD requirement IDs\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Define a FileInfo struct that exposes modification time (time.Time), access time\n          (time.Time), block count (int64), and block size (int64) with consistent field names\n          across Darwin and Linux. Include the original os.FileInfo so callers can access standard\n          fields (Name, Size, Mode, IsDir). Implement Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) and\n          Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) that call os.Stat/os.Lstat, extract the underlying\n          syscall.Stat_t via a platform-specific helper, and populate all FileInfo fields.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement TerminalSize(fd uintptr) (*WinSize, error) that queries terminal dimensions\n          via the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl using golang.org/x/sys/unix. WinSize must have Width (columns)\n          and Height (rows) fields, both uint16. Return a descriptive error when fd is not a\n          terminal.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Isolate all platform-specific Stat_t field access into build-tagged files:\n          fileinfo_darwin.go with //go:build darwin and fileinfo_linux.go with //go:build linux.\n          Each platform file implements an extractFileInfo function that takes a syscall.Stat_t\n          pointer and returns the platform-specific time and block fields. The shared fileinfo.go\n          and terminal.go must not import platform-specific packages directly.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Use golang.org/x/sys/unix for ioctl operations and TIOCGWINSZ constant. If go.mod does\n          not already include golang.org/x/sys, add it via go get. Do not use the deprecated\n          syscall package where golang.org/x/sys/unix provides the equivalent.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"golang.org/x/sys is the only approved external dependency per ARCHITECTURE.yaml. cmd/ packages must not import golang.org/x/sys directly -- they import pkg/sys as the abstraction layer.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Primary source files named after their primary exported type per project convention: fileinfo.go for FileInfo, terminal.go for WinSize. Platform-specific files use _darwin/_linux suffixes.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Follow coding style from pkg/testutils/difftest.go: copyright header with year and author, SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT, package doc comment, Implements comment referencing PRD requirement IDs.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/sys/fileinfo.go exports FileInfo struct, Stat function, and Lstat function with documented signatures\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"pkg/sys/fileinfo_darwin.go has //go:build darwin tag and extracts Mtimespec, Atimespec, and Blocks from Darwin Stat_t\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"pkg/sys/fileinfo_linux.go has //go:build linux tag and extracts Mtim, Atim, and Blocks from Linux Stat_t\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"pkg/sys/terminal.go exports WinSize struct and TerminalSize function\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/sys/ succeeds with no errors on the current platform\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/sys/ reports no issues\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"c5f11b65-15ac-4000-ba8b-5da79c48538f","total_cost_usd":0.4791065,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":38193,"output_tokens":18400,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18400,"cacheReadInputTokens":38193,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4791065,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"d8b8acd4-6682-4f98-b11a-0781c720888d"}
